+E.1 How to use this companion
+
+  Three colours, three kinds of statement
+
+   • Guaranteed by construction (solid blue in the diagrams): true for every run, proved in
+       Proposition 4.1 or asserted in code. Say “guaranteed”.
+
+   • Encouraged by design (dashed blue): the method pushes in this direction but promises no
+       value. Say “encouraged” or “by design”.
+
+   • Measured empirically (orange): a number from one corpus, with its control. Say “on this
+       corpus we measured”.
+
+  Memory aids
+
+   • “S up, F down, T either way.” What each term does at every merge.
+   • “Times three.” 12 → 40 → 120: each level is about three times finer.
+   • “MiniLM builds, BGE judges, DeBERTa checks the words.” The three models and their
+
+       roles.
+   • “Regularise is the cause, matching is the name tag.” λT changes the clusters; Hungarian
+
+       matching only names them.
+   • “Propose with pairs, pay with hyperedges.” Candidate pairs come from co-membership; the
+
+       cost uses native multiplicities.
+   • “Floor, not force.” p = 1/101 is the smallest value 100 nulls can give.
+   • “Blind, not robust.” Semantic-only perturbation ARI of 1 means it never looks at edges.
+   • “Evidence hit is not identity hit.” Why retrieval scores 0/63.
+   • “Budget met is not balanced.” One L0 super-node holds 65% of the nodes.
+
+  Drawing the whole model on paper in one minute
+
+   1. Timeline. Four boxes: 2020, 2022, 2024, 2026. Between neighbours write “λT ” above the arrow
+       and “match ids” below it (Figure 16).
+
+   2. Funnel. Under one box: |Vt| → 120 → 40 → 12 with an upward arrow labelled “merges only”
+       (Figure 11).
+
+   3. Triangle. S, F , T at the corners, J in the middle, and α, 1 − α, λ on the spokes (Figure 12).
+   4. One blob. Five dots in a dashed outline, an arrow, and {A:3, B:1, C:1} (Figure 15).
+   5. One dashed vertical line. Left: MiniLM, 70% of members, predictions. Right: BGE with nulls,
+
+       30% with NLI, gold (Figure 18).
