+Why a merge is cheap: every statistic is additive
+
+After merging A and B into C, Merger.run does four additions and nothing else: count[c] =
+count[a] + count[b], sums[c] = sums[a] + sums[b], inc[c] = inc[a] + inc[b] (edge multi-
+plicities) and previous[c] = previous[a] + previous[b] (history counts). No member is revisited.
+The new cluster’s neighbours are the union of the parents’ neighbours, and one fresh ∆J is pushed
+for each of them.
