+Q8. What is the difference between origin_year and first_seen_year?
+30-second answer. origin_year is when the thing was introduced in the world. first_seen_year
+is the earliest corpus paper that mentions it. TSHC uses first_seen_year for visibility, because a
+snapshot at year t may only assert what the corpus had seen by t.
+If they push further.
+• This distinction is the hook for P6 temporal honesty named in the task.
+• Surface forms and pretrained language models are not historically versioned (a stated limitation).
+Common trap. Using origin_year would let a 2020 snapshot contain an entity the corpus first
+mentions in 2024.
