+Q23. What is the temporal term T ?
+
+30-second answer. T is the VI between the current partition and the previous snapshot’s partition
+at the same level, restricted to nodes present in both snapshots and divided by 2 log |Ut|. New nodes
+contribute nothing, because they have no history to be faithful to.
+If they push further.
+• It is level-specific: the 40 → 12 stage is regularised towards the previous level-0 partition.
+• Only the temporal variant uses it.
+• Since VI ≤ log n (§2.5), T is in fact at most 0.5; the constant only rescales λ.
