+\noindent\sclab{Events can overlap.} Identity (continuation or growth) comes from the one-to-one
+Hungarian match. Merge and split come from the full many-to-many overlap table. So one new
+cluster can be a \emph{growth} (it inherits the id of its best match) and at the same time the
+target of a \emph{merge} (it strongly overlaps two old clusters). That is why the event counts of
+a transition can exceed 172, the number of super-nodes per snapshot. The events describe
+membership changes, not scientific history.
