+\vspace{8pt}
+\begin{minipage}[t]{0.47\linewidth}
+\sctrap{Eight things not to overclaim}\par\vspace{1pt}
+\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=1.3em,itemsep=1.5pt,topsep=0pt,parsep=0pt]
+  \item A greedy heuristic, not a global optimum.
+  \item 12/40/120 are display budgets, not natural community counts.
+  \item Temporal does not win every metric at every transition.
+  \item Null effects are small in absolute terms; $p=1/101$ is a floor.
+  \item NLI is a proxy, not expert validation.
+  \item Flat and hierarchy both have zero complete top-10 and top-25 target recall.
+  \item Comparison count is not latency.
+  \item Benchmark and claim alignment are limited; the benchmark was inspected.
+\end{enumerate}
+\end{minipage}\hfill
+\begin{minipage}[t]{0.49\linewidth}
+\sclab{Eight one-line answers}\par\vspace{1pt}
+\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=1.3em,itemsep=1.5pt,topsep=0pt,parsep=0pt]
+  \item \textbf{Global optimum?} No: each step is the best current candidate.
+  \item \textbf{Why hypergraph-native?} Projection loses edge identity, arity and grouping.
+  \item \textbf{What causes stability?} $\lambda T$ in the objective; matching only names.
+  \item \textbf{Circularity?} MiniLM builds, BGE judges, nulls; held-out labels; hashed predictions.
+  \item \textbf{Why $p=0.0099$ everywhere?} The floor of 100 nulls; effects are 0.003--0.011.
+  \item \textbf{Does it help retrieval?} Not shown: 0/63 for every system.
+  \item \textbf{Semantic ARI of 1?} Edge-blind, not robust.
+  \item \textbf{Next?} Expert audits, held-out questions, then pre-registered fixes.
+\end{enumerate}
+\end{minipage}
